<title>BELGIUM: GERMANY MAY MISS DEBT, DEFICIT CRITERIA - ISSING.</title>
<headline>GERMANY MAY MISS DEBT, DEFICIT CRITERIA - ISSING.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank board member Otmar Issing said on Friday that Germany's budget deficit may rise to nearly four percent this year and that government debt could exceed the Maastricht criteria of 60 percent of GDP.</p>
<p>&quot;From the present point of view it cannot be precluded that the government deficit in the current year rises to nearly four percent,&quot; Issing told the annual general assembly of the European Mortgage Federation.</p>
<p>&quot;In 1995, Germany remained only just under the Maastricht criterion of 60 percent for government debt; this year this threshhold may even be exceeded,&quot; he said. -- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287-6830</p>
</text>
